                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "662609ee-a19d-3bd8-abbf-95c1eae67af0",
                        "entry_id": "03a00138-ffc3-34a8-82ae-a1092ddfaa70",
                        "glosses": [
                            "van een persoon dat deze somber en wat bozig is"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dea7692c-637c-4cb7-8ee9-0d2be14b0b9b",
                                "sense_id": "662609ee-a19d-3bd8-abbf-95c1eae67af0",
                                "text": "We gingen aan de slootkant zitten, onder de parasol. Om kwart over vier liepen twee mannen aan, de leptosoom (Max geheten) en een jongere gast een kop kleiner. Met een morose gezichtsuitdrukking en een grafstem maakte deze zich bekend als Herman. Hij had de torso en de armen van een gewichtheffer, vol tatoeages."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fdabdd4-7ba3-44da-927d-a3e1d1967a74",
                                "sense_id": "662609ee-a19d-3bd8-abbf-95c1eae67af0",
                                "text": "Met morose trekken en ongeduldige vingers begon Jean-Luc aan een van de uiteinden van het pakpapier te frunniken en probeerde het te scheuren, maar dat gaf blijkbaar niet zo makkelijk mee. Hij vloekte en bloosde."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d331174c-09da-41d1-82a7-9a2baa7feec9",
                                "sense_id": "662609ee-a19d-3bd8-abbf-95c1eae67af0",
                                "text": "Vier sterren voor de uitvoering. Alleen: het voelt niet goed. Wij werden er thuis collectief morose van. De Welcome is apparatus non grata verklaard en zit weer in de doos."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2870c38a-a3f7-47b4-aad0-e4c90dc527b9",
                        "source_entry_id": "03a00138-ffc3-34a8-82ae-a1092ddfaa70",
                        "source_sense_id": "662609ee-a19d-3bd8-abbf-95c1eae67af0",
                        "source_sense_description": "op een stille manier bozig zijn",
                        "target_lang_word": "angry",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "angry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                        "entry_id": "fb214066-1c6e-3c6f-8e30-c926cead0053",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Displaying or feeling anger."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e627095-0d09-4d1b-82db-ca53fd522432",
                                                "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                                "text": "His face became angry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fe1a279-0271-4cc1-9ff0-28acb18e2866",
                                                "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                                "text": "An angry mob started looting the warehouse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bd8dd38-bd09-4894-89e5-fccd1807f552",
                                                "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                                "text": "Then we relapsed into a discomfited silence, and wished we were anywhere else. But Miss Thorn relieved the situation by laughing aloud, and with such a hearty enjoyment that instead of getting angry and more mortified we began to laugh ourselves, and instantly felt better."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2961ed0-eeea-4c3d-8b8e-1d8593564a9f",
                                                "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                                "text": "Cone, who once called himself “the angriest theologian in America,” is still angry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0724fe9-669d-4ee8-9e18-0165a2766828",
                                                "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                                "text": "But, statistically-speaking, there is significantly-greater-than-even odds of the American forces coming out victorious - as I said, largely due to, one, the sheer technology advantage of the radar and fire-control systems, and also two, the almighty swarm of Fletchers. Never, ever underestimate the firepower of an almighty swarm of angry Fletchers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d86fc7c-9206-4612-b12e-f4938275c0e6",
                                                "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                                "text": "I kept my window rolled up, eyes on the road, probably making the pickup man angrier with my silence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5da46532-5dac-4837-9f6c-4c899ea3f426",
                                                "sense_id": "897eba31-13e2-3db2-831e-aaabc56f9f6a",
                                                "text": "All considered, never going to bed angry sounds like a good rule to live by. But it isn’t always useful, Romanoff said."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab203b54-7958-33da-8397-38aaee139820",
                                        "entry_id": "fb214066-1c6e-3c6f-8e30-c926cead0053",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inflamed and painful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "said about a wound or a rash"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9eaffc95-a04c-4e23-892c-45ec86a8dc7f",
                                                "sense_id": "ab203b54-7958-33da-8397-38aaee139820",
                                                "text": "The broken glass left two angry cuts across my arm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7538fbd8-6e41-34c4-89e3-a2581ce1b99d",
                                        "entry_id": "fb214066-1c6e-3c6f-8e30-c926cead0053",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dark and stormy, menacing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c16f932b-adf4-4483-8933-8561b6e5aa11",
                                                "sense_id": "7538fbd8-6e41-34c4-89e3-a2581ce1b99d",
                                                "text": "Angry clouds raced across the sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1dde35ca-ff45-44a2-9721-7904f6013914",
                                                "sense_id": "7538fbd8-6e41-34c4-89e3-a2581ce1b99d",
                                                "text": "[…]nor dreads he the angry sea[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59bdfc48-636a-4f2d-a5c7-0489e287d9d8",
                                                "sense_id": "7538fbd8-6e41-34c4-89e3-a2581ce1b99d",
                                                "text": "When she and her sister were away at Williamsburg, Nancy and I were more like founderers on a raft adrift in an angry sea."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "angry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                        "entry_id": "3adc8ead-d3cd-3f35-9d98-78c5d6bc6898",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To anger."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2035e78-60f0-4463-b9dd-6ab40eaec44e",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "Onely they that repent, and are verie ſorie that they haue angried God with their ſinnes, and yet truſt that they are forgiuẽ them for Chriſtes ſake, and that the reſt of their weakeneſſe and vnperfectnes is couered with his deth & paſſion, who alſo deſire to goe forwarde and growe more and more in holy life & conuerſation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "748d6825-2349-4b25-a8be-359d810d64d8",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "The King ſent to the Londoners requeſting to borrowe of them one thouſande pounde, whiche they ſtoutely denyed, and alſo euil entreated, bette and néere hand ſlew a certain Lumbard that woulde haue lent the King the ſayde ſumme, which when the King heard he was maruellouſly angried, and calling togither almoſt all the nobles of the lande, hée opened to them the malitiouſneſſe of the Londoners, and cõplayned of theyr preſumption, the whyche noble men gaue counſell, that their inſolencie ſhoulde with ſpéede be oppreſſed, and theyr pride abated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52818a0b-ec27-4f9f-b76e-f30007ed025f",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "For when the Arabians being offended with Heraclius for denying them their pay, and for his religion had ſeuered themſelues from him, Mahomet ioyned himſelfe to the angried ſouldiers, and ſtirred vp their minds againſt their Emperour, and encouraged them in their defection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7329e784-e80b-43e7-b32b-491e6c116a7b",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "For verily the common ſort (O Socratus my friende,) is ingratefull, full of mockes and ſcornes, vaine, ſoone angried, cruel, enuious, rude, heaped full of troubles and trifles: and whoſeuer doth familiarly acquaint himſelfe with them, & conuerſe amongſt them, doth at the length, become farre more miſerable then they be themſelues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f56aa3b0-5431-4a76-a461-e3a051e7b63b",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "I doe well to be angry. It was a milde ſaying of Auguſtus the Emperour to one of his ſouldiers deſirous to be diſmiſſed his armie, but wanting a iuſt and honeſt excuſe to his friends at his returne home, ſay, ſaith the Emperour, that I have angried thee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f995a8b-8bc4-4d06-bfa7-8a95212216d2",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "It is the doctrin of the Scripture. that our good works are alwaies ſtained with much vncleanes, with which God may be iuſtly offended and angried: ſo farre are they from purchazing vs his good will, or prouoking his liberalitie towards vs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "867c067a-0509-4278-822e-249898871681",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "And what Potiphars wife ſaid with her tongue, ſhe ſaith unto the paſſengers with her geſture and gate, Come lie with me; and nothing angrieth her ſo much, as when modeſt men affect a deafneſſe and will not heare, or a dulneſſe and will not underſtand the language of her behaviour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "494d6835-bfb6-44c4-baa9-b030c7c170df",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "Even thy Creatures, how terrible are they, O Lord! all hearts are afraid of thy tempeſts, and melt at thy ſtormes: O let me in this glaſſe of their terror ſee the dreadfull face of thy angried Majeſtie! at which the depths themſelves doe tremble, and the foundations of the world are diſcovered, even as the blaſt of the breath of thy noſtrils, O Lord! And let me never preſume to exalt my ſelfe againſt thee, but ever tremble before thy face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cac9dddb-3484-476e-990c-500f3e475210",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "Yet I am both (replyed ſhe) for my joyes at what he hath done, proceeds principally from his angrying me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2e388cf-1a89-4a55-bab3-1923b3df4e44",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "Palanice cannot ſpeak unto Cercinea in behalf of Clorian, without angrying me in the perſon of Alcander, and unleſſe ſhe oblige me to raviſh Amilcar from her; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cab5d95-eb47-4e2d-939f-ce62cfc9b535",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "King Ahab was a good ſervant of the devil, but Ahab had angried God, and God was reſolved he would ſpare him no longer, but cut him off."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d373281a-b460-4820-b14d-07592ef9e135",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "What doth the repeating thoſe verbs import, but angrying bitterly or grievouſly?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a60bccf-bb1d-4483-b9df-d0996cdf282c",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "But the truth was, thoſe former Committees durſt not attempt ſuch a change of their Affairs, for fear of the charge of ſuch a remove; but eſpecially for fear of angrying the Mogul, whoſe people gained exceedingly by our ſhips riding in their Ports, as well as by our Trade, and were out of fear of Bombay, while it was in ſuch a forlorn neglected condition; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "503c3d70-da24-4fbb-ac2a-b5bebf100332",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "IT angrying a Country-man to ſee his two Hogs often fighting together, he killed one of them; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abd89bef-8ef5-4007-8b56-9677d644d189",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "And this End of God is now made void when ſinners repent not: Men are ſometimes grieved, and ſometimes angried when they are diſappointed in their End; o is God ſaid to be: He complains often of this in the Scriptures, when he is diſappointed in the End of his Corrections; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9a76286-3a75-4217-93f9-a02a158b179e",
                                                "sense_id": "9b445b66-f7ac-3dd7-a43d-324d854cde95",
                                                "text": "Our temperate Sage, though angried at that spirit of contradiction which he had raised, must, however, have sometimes smiled both on his advocates and his adversaries!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1109a5bc-9adc-41d5-8ad5-4b527daefb62",
                        "source_entry_id": "03a00138-ffc3-34a8-82ae-a1092ddfaa70",
                        "source_sense_id": "662609ee-a19d-3bd8-abbf-95c1eae67af0",
                        "source_sense_description": "op een stille manier bozig zijn",
                        "target_lang_word": "silent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "silent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a08eedd-a886-3854-a1e7-2bfd6837c578",
                                        "entry_id": "917731ad-5efd-3dcc-b5de-a8e41afa46e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Free from sound or noise; absolutely still; perfectly quiet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c160ae1-66dd-4680-ab26-b0a21b9e2d7d",
                                                "sense_id": "3a08eedd-a886-3854-a1e7-2bfd6837c578",
                                                "text": "How silent is this town!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7acc4c74-b835-457e-b2b8-e9e824e1b8a0",
                                                "sense_id": "3a08eedd-a886-3854-a1e7-2bfd6837c578",
                                                "text": "What was formerly performed by fleets and armies, by invasions, sieges, and battles, has been of late accomplished by more silent methods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "965a553a-3af5-4cf3-9693-ef4aeb40be0a",
                                                "sense_id": "3a08eedd-a886-3854-a1e7-2bfd6837c578",
                                                "text": "The voice of the auctioneer is slow and low […]; after a pause, which seems no silenter than the rest of the transaction, he ceases to repeat the bids, and his fish, in the measure of a bushel or so, have gone for a matter of three shillings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6535091f-8df5-3ddf-bdbe-3155efcd5db6",
                                        "entry_id": "917731ad-5efd-3dcc-b5de-a8e41afa46e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not speaking; indisposed to talk; speechless; mute; taciturn; not loquacious; not talkative."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a40131d-d9dc-495d-8025-5e9e1583e285",
                                                "sense_id": "6535091f-8df5-3ddf-bdbe-3155efcd5db6",
                                                "text": "Ulysses, adds he, was the most eloquent and most silent of men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f34e719-aeaa-4ade-a93a-531ce94b04e8",
                                                "sense_id": "6535091f-8df5-3ddf-bdbe-3155efcd5db6",
                                                "text": "This new-created world, whereof in hell / Fame is not silent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fc86d75-583e-4cad-8171-26b42d5f7fd4",
                                                "sense_id": "6535091f-8df5-3ddf-bdbe-3155efcd5db6",
                                                "text": "Tothero is silent before replying. His great strength is in these silences; he has the disciplinarian's trick of waiting a long moment while his words gather weight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf12ccd6-f028-3007-83ca-e53605012142",
                                        "entry_id": "917731ad-5efd-3dcc-b5de-a8e41afa46e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Keeping at rest; inactive; calm; undisturbed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf757c57-d59b-40d3-8e79-58812285856a",
                                                "sense_id": "bf12ccd6-f028-3007-83ca-e53605012142",
                                                "text": "The winds were silent, all the waves asleep, / And heaven was trac'd upon the flattering deep"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c35f95f-ae89-3f83-bb79-a6ca4e6ef423",
                                        "entry_id": "917731ad-5efd-3dcc-b5de-a8e41afa46e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not pronounced; having no sound; quiescent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a384c13d-e93b-4b5f-8370-49d635e262d0",
                                                "sense_id": "3c35f95f-ae89-3f83-bb79-a6ca4e6ef423",
                                                "text": "The e is silent in fable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3f98b41-d456-4711-9287-09d227c19f0e",
                                                "sense_id": "3c35f95f-ae89-3f83-bb79-a6ca4e6ef423",
                                                "text": "Silent letters can make some words difficult to spell."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "632d9d8a-3487-4b30-95f4-3afb93271fa1",
                                                "sense_id": "3c35f95f-ae89-3f83-bb79-a6ca4e6ef423",
                                                "text": "The l in the English word salmon is silent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19d649a6-cc67-3891-b247-2c272e1f9f3b",
                                        "entry_id": "917731ad-5efd-3dcc-b5de-a8e41afa46e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having no effect; not operating; inefficient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fe4c7b1-f755-42c2-924a-2d00f8271212",
                                                "sense_id": "19d649a6-cc67-3891-b247-2c272e1f9f3b",
